The containers reach your SonarQube over TLS at `${sonarqube_url}`, through the proxy in
`sonarqube-tls-proxy/`. Run that proxy on your SonarQube machine: copy the directory there and
follow its `README.md`. It forwards to SonarQube on port ${sonarqube_port} of that machine, and its
certificate for `${sonarqube_host}` is signed by this bundle's CA, which the containers trust.

Only the containers use the proxy: your users and scanners keep reaching SonarQube as they do
today. If SonarQube doesn't listen on port ${sonarqube_port}, or `${sonarqube_host}` doesn't resolve
to its machine from the containers, regenerate this bundle with `--sonarqube-external-host` and
`--sonarqube-external-port` set correctly.
